-- Q12321: Statement of Cash Flows [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 230-10-45-15(b), repayments of amounts borrowed are classified as financing activities. A principal payment on a bank loan reduces outstanding debt, which is a transaction with creditors squarely within financing.
Wrong (A): Operating activities relate to the entity''s core revenue-generating functions, not to debt principal repayments.
Wrong (C): Investing activities involve purchases and disposals of long-term assets or investments, not repayment of borrowed funds.
Wrong (D): Classification does not depend on how the loan proceeds were originally used; all principal debt repayments are financing regardless of purpose.$EXPL$
