-- Q12322: Statement of Cash Flows [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 230-10-45-12 and ASC 842, when a sale-leaseback qualifies as a sale, the full $1,500,000 cash received is reported as an investing inflow. The $300,000 gain is removed from operating activities under the indirect method to avoid double-counting.
Wrong (A): This incorrectly limits the investing inflow to the book value. The cash flow statement reports actual cash proceeds, not the carrying amount of the asset sold.
Wrong (B): The $300,000 gain is not reported separately as an investing inflow; the full sale price represents the cash received.
Wrong (C): A qualifying sale-leaseback is not a noncash transaction. Cash was received for the asset; the leaseback is a separate operating lease arrangement.$EXPL$
