Wrong (A): Escrow deposits for asset purchases are not operating activities. Operating outflows relate to day-to-day revenue-generating activities, not capital asset acquisitions.
Wrong (B): Financing activities involve transactions with creditors and owners. An escrow deposit for a real estate purchase is an investing activity.
