-- Q12341: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 250-10-45-23, this non-counterbalancing error requires restatement. The patent should have been capitalized at $150,000 and amortized $10,000/year for 3 years. Entry: Dr. Patent $150,000, Cr. Accumulated Amortization $30,000, Cr. Retained Earnings $120,000. RE was understated by $120,000 ($150,000 expensed minus $30,000 proper amortization).
Wrong (A): This entry has the same debits and credits but omits the critical conclusion that RE is understated by $120,000. The incomplete answer fails to address the RE impact.
Wrong (B): Debiting Patent at $120,000 omits the gross asset and accumulated amortization presentation. The patent must be recorded at its original $150,000 cost with separate accumulated amortization.
Wrong (D): "Prior Period Adjustment" is not a separate account; the credit goes to Retained Earnings. Additionally, stating RE is overstated is directionally wrong -- RE was understated by the excess expense.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12341;

-- Q12343: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [easy/L1]
