UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 250-10-20, indirect effects are changes to current or future cash flows that result from applying a change in accounting principle retrospectively, such as royalty payments or profit-sharing contributions that change because restated income differs.
Wrong (B): Changes to prior-period financial statement line items from restating the method are direct effects of the change, not indirect effects.
Wrong (C): The cumulative effect on retained earnings at the beginning of the earliest period is a direct mechanical result of retrospective application, not an indirect effect.
Wrong (D): Adjustments to comparative per-share amounts are direct effects that flow automatically from restated income figures, not indirect cash flow consequences.$EXPL$
