-- Q12346: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 250-10-45-23 and 250-10-50-7, when prior-period statements are not presented, the entity adjusts the opening balance of retained earnings for the earliest period presented (Year 2 opening) and discloses the nature and effect of the error.
Wrong (B): Error corrections are never reported as current-period income or expense. Charging $60,000 to Year 2 income would distort that period''s operating results.
Wrong (C): Correction is always required regardless of whether prior-period statements are presented comparatively. ASC 250 mandates adjustment to opening RE.
Wrong (D): There is no concept of a contra-equity account for error corrections in U.S. GAAP. Errors are corrected through retained earnings, not amortized over time.$EXPL$
