-- Q12347: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 250-10-45-2, any voluntary change in accounting principle requires justification that the new method is preferable. SEC registrants must also obtain a preferability letter from their independent auditor per Regulation S-X Rule 10-01(b)(6). Changing back shortly after switching faces heightened scrutiny.
Wrong (A): ASC 250 does not permit unrestricted voluntary changes. Each change must be justified as preferable under the circumstances, and SEC registrants need auditor concurrence.
Wrong (C): There is no permanent prohibition on reverting to a previously used method. The standard requires a preferability demonstration, not a lifetime ban.
Wrong (D): Reverting to a previously used method does not exempt the entity from the preferability assessment or the auditor''s letter requirement.$EXPL$
