-- Q12362: Consolidations [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25-3(e) and ASC 810-10-45, when intercompany profit is eliminated in consolidation, the tax already paid by the seller must be deferred. The seller paid tax on $200,000 profit, creating a $200,000 x 40% = $80,000 deferred tax asset (prepaid tax from a consolidated perspective).
Wrong (A): A deferred tax liability is directionally wrong. Tax was overpaid relative to consolidated income (which shows no profit), so the deferred balance is an asset, not a liability.
Wrong (B): A deferred tax adjustment is required whenever intercompany profit is eliminated. Ignoring the tax effect would misstate both consolidated tax expense and deferred taxes.
Wrong (C): The $120,000 figure incorrectly applies the 40% rate to $300,000 (cost) instead of the $200,000 intercompany profit that was eliminated.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12362;

-- Q12363: Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 810-10-45-23, changes in a parent''s ownership interest while control is retained are equity transactions. NCI is reduced by its carrying amount ($480,000), and the $120,000 excess of consideration paid over NCI carrying amount reduces APIC (or retained earnings if APIC is insufficient).
Wrong (B): No gain or loss is recognized in earnings for ownership changes while control is maintained. ASC 810 treats these as transactions between owners recorded entirely in equity.
Wrong (C): Goodwill is not adjusted for post-acquisition ownership changes under ASC 810. Goodwill adjustments apply only at the initial acquisition date.
Wrong (D): Reducing NCI by the full $600,000 ignores that NCI''s carrying amount is only $480,000. The $120,000 difference must be charged to equity, not attributed to NCI.$EXPL$
