-- Q12368: Consolidations [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 810-10-45-5, when a subsidiary holds shares of its parent, those shares are reported as treasury stock in the consolidated financial statements. From a consolidated perspective, the group has effectively reacquired its own shares.
Wrong (B): The consolidated entity cannot hold a marketable equity investment in itself. Fair value treatment as a security is inappropriate for parent shares held within the group.
Wrong (C): The equity method is used for investments in other entities, not for a subsidiary''s holdings of its own parent''s stock. The consolidated entity treats these as its own shares.
Wrong (D): Reducing NCI is incorrect because the subsidiary''s purchase of parent stock does not change the parent''s ownership percentage in the subsidiary.$EXPL$
