-- Q12369: Consolidations [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 323-10-40-1, when an investee issues shares at a price above book value per share, the investor''s proportionate share of the investee''s total net assets increases even though its ownership percentage decreases. Beacon recognizes a dilution gain equal to the increase in its share of Spectral''s underlying equity.
Wrong (A): An adjustment is required even though Beacon did not sell shares. The investee''s issuance above book value changes the investor''s claim on net assets, triggering gain recognition.
Wrong (C): A write-down for dilution loss would apply only if shares were issued below book value, reducing Beacon''s share of net assets. Here, issuance was above book value.
Wrong (D): Reclassification to fair value through net income is not warranted. Beacon retains significant influence and continues to apply the equity method.$EXPL$
