-- Q12371: Consolidations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 810-10-45, the $20,000 constructive retirement gain is recognized in full in Year 1 consolidated statements. In subsequent years, the parent''s premium amortization and subsidiary''s discount amortization both approach par, causing equal annual reversals of the gain through interest expense and income adjustments over the remaining 3 years.
Wrong (B): While the gain is recognized in Year 1, subsequent years require eliminating entries that reverse portions of the gain through interest adjustments. The process is not complete in Year 1.
Wrong (C): Goodwill is unrelated to constructive retirement gains. The gain arises from the difference between carrying amount and purchase price, not from a business combination.
